\"This report describes progress toward World Health Assembly milestones and measles elimination objectives during 2000–2020\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"calculated by dividing the number of vaccine doses administered by the estimated target population, reported annually\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"to incorporate alternative assumptions of correlation between routine MCV doses and SIAs and updated case-fatality ratios\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Any country not reporting measles cases for that year was removed from both the numerator and denominator in calculating incidence.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Deaths prevented by vaccination are estimated by the area between estimated deaths with vaccination and without vaccination\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"The discarded case rate is used to measure the sensitivity of measles surveillance.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}